{"text": "282111129\n\nSTATE OF INDIANA\nOFFICE OF THE ATTORNEY GENERAL\n\nINDIANA GOVERNMENT CENTER SOUTH, FIFTH FLOOR\n\n402 WEST WASHINGTON STREET = INDIANAPOLIS, IN 462062770\nJEFFREY A. MODISETT \u2018TELEPHONE GID) 28-4201\nATTORNEY GENERAL October 22, 1999\n\u2018Neil Mellon\nGeneral Counsel\nMSA Compliance\n\nBrowa & Williamson Tohacea\n200 Brown & Williamson Tower\n401 S. 4\" Avenue\nP.O. Box 35090\nLouisville, KY 40232\n\nRe: Oct. 4 meeting\nDear Mr. Mellon\n\n| would like to thank you and your colleagues at Brown & Williamson who met\nwith me, Attorney General Miller, and the representatives for the Attorneys General of\nOhio, Kentucky, and California. it was very helpful to mect the people who make the\nultimate decisions regarding the advertising strategy for your company and its products,\nIt was especially valuable to learn of the process involved internally in making such\ndecisions,\n\nIt is apparent that the people who met with us believe strongly that your company\nis marketing its products to consumers from the ages of 21-30, and older. I think we all\nagreed that even advertising targeted at this age group might bleed over and have a major\nimpact on an even younger category of consumers \u2014 including many under the age of 18,\nThope it was obvious to you and everyone we met (indeed, Attomey General Miller\npointed this out several times during our meeting), the primary focus of the attorneys\ngeneral concern remains the impact of the advertising of cigarettes on minors.\n\nwould like to summarize for you some of my thoughts and impressions of the\nmeetings we had on October 4, 1999,\n\n(1) Everyone we met with stated that your company does not try to entice\n\u2018non-sinokers to use your products, but that you only \u201ctarget\u201d smokers\nbetween the ages of 21-30 to use your products. We discussed at length\nthe agpropriateness of the \u201cB-Kool\u201d campaign. While your intentions\nneni\naes\ngot 27 we\n\n@ wes\n\nPRODUCED FROM B&W